// Locks in two dyn corners beyond the basic [&dyn / Box<dyn>] cases:
//
//   * `pinned` — `Pin<Box<dyn Future<Output=u32>>>`. The Pin
//     specialization peels the wrapper at parse time; the renderer
//     re-applies the outer Pin<…> ident so the user keeps seeing
//     they're looking at a pinned reference. Future's vtable
//     concrete is an opaque `{{closure}}` (the async coroutine);
//     value-inline doesn't fire for closures.
//   * `dyn_iter` — `Box<dyn Iterator<Item=u32>>`. Iterator's dyn
//     vtable is small (most methods are `where Self: Sized` and
//     therefore not dyn-compatible) but exercises both the
//     `<Concrete as Trait>::override` shape (next, size_hint) and
//     the `Iterator::default_impl` shape (advance_by, nth) for
//     trait-grouping detection.

{ jsonrpc: "2.0", id: 1, method: "break.set", params: { at: "main.rs:173" } }
{ jsonrpc: "2.0", id: 2, method: "run" }
